WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
See working, quiet and CI-waiting sessions across agent tools and projects.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.000
The tablet keeps the roster, activity timeline and usage windows in view.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Select a session to focus its timeline. CI waiting does not mean approval is needed.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Explicit reply requests have a waiting timer. A one-way notification stays a notification.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Reported usage windows and reset times appear on the dashboard and dedicated dials.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:14.033
Original question → choice → one-time permission → resumed work. This is the real local control path.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:24.033
Keys surface sessions and supported answers. Dials keep usage accessible without taking over every key.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:32.033
Available controls follow the connected agent. Unsupported sessions remain observation-only.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:41.033
Task review separates an AI estimate from verified evidence and from your own assessment.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:50.033
Read the original request, reply and tool evidence. Your correction stays separate from the AI judgement.

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:59.033
E-ink prioritizes readable status. Controls depend on the device and the connected agent's capabilities.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:08.033
A small display does not promise a full controller. Its useful status and input scope are device-specific.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:16.033
Timebox, iDotMatrix and TC001 are glance displays; they do not promise touch approval.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:24.033
The local hub connects your own screens. Additional hardware is optional.
